 "caveats": [
  "reporter_ion_mz is THEORETICAL, charge 1: a DI HCD diagnostic-ion mass from mzLib's embedded TMT.txt plus one proton. It is not a calibrated or observed value.",
  "mz_min and mz_max are reporter_ion_mz -/+ absolute_tolerance (0.003 Da, the window mzLib takes from doi:10.1021/acs.jproteome.1c00168). mzLib uses the same window to read reporter intensities from a spectrum, keeping the most intense peak inside it.",
  "TMT16 and TMT18 are TMTpro. TMT16 is the lowest sixteen channels of the TMTpro 18-plex set and has no modification entry of its own, so its m/z are TMT18's first sixteen.",
  "iTRAQ8 has no 120 channel: the phenylalanine immonium ion sits at 120.081, so the eighth reagent is 121.",
  "channel_index is 0-based and ascends with reporter_ion_mz; channel_label at that index names the channel whose reporter ion it is."
 ]
}
